","limitations":["The cause of node1's ssh.service/ssh.socket failure at the final snapshot is not established from the evidence — no executor command explicitly stopped or modified sshd, so it could be an environmental artifact of the reboot process or ufw interaction, but it cannot be ruled out as executor-caused.","No evidence captures whether ssh.service recovered after the after_executor snapshot, since that is the last observation in the record.","The executor's post-node1-reboot verification only re-tested port 9000 connectivity from node2/node3, not SSH itself, so the intermediate 'SSH reachable' claim for that specific window relies on a broader test taken later from node3 (cmd-abe31b1dd9c24fdc), not a dedicated node1-reboot SSH check."]},"ttft_ms":29556,"type":"result","duration_ms":86334,"uuid":"bc136f19-b34f-45d9-9e7d-3bda237f4ce1","ttft_stream_ms":805,"time_to_request_ms":56,"first_content_frame_ms":805,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
